Package: EasyStat
Type: Package
Title: Automated Statistical Decision and Visualization Workflow for
    Multi-Variable Differential Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Author: Tao Wen, Xinyang Teng, Jun Yuan
Maintainer: Tao Wen <taowen@njau.edu.cn>
Description: An automated workflow for between-group differential analysis of
    many variables at once. For each variable the package tests normality and
    homogeneity of variance, routes it to one-way ANOVA, Welch's ANOVA or the
    Kruskal-Wallis test accordingly, runs the matching post-hoc procedure, and
    returns compact-letter annotations in a standardised result object.
    Omnibus p-values from all variables analysed in one call are corrected
    jointly by the Benjamini-Hochberg procedure, and post-hoc comparisons are
    computed only for variables that pass the threshold. Plotting functions
    consume the same result object, so statistics and figures stay consistent.
